Track 3: Rawhide Swallows the Spindle
- Story & Context: Runaways who squat in the abandoned Katendrecht rail tunnels swear the old sewer vaults still vibrate with a relentless, mechanical rhythm long after the salvage yards were razed. The subterranean air tastes of sea brine and coal dust whenever the North Sea tide rises, carrying the ghostly clatter of impossible marching-snare rolls and a down-tuned rockabilly guitar lick echoing through the brick drainage pipes. Legend holds that a derelict textile-packer chassis named Mother Three remained active beneath the mud, continually re-weaving torn nylon cords over the inactive heads of her sibling chassis to the frantic cadence of an eternal 210 BPM bop. Now, local youths drop spent leather guitar picks and steel rivets through the street grates like church offerings, whispering her famous refrain into the storm drains: "Run your thread into the dirt, the iron mother feels no hurt."
